I ran into this case:
```c++
/// See nvtt::Container.
typedef enum
{
	NVTT_Container_DDS,
	NVTT_Container_DDS10,
} NvttContainer;
```

The naive common prefixer would remove `NVTT_Container_DDS`, creating a zero-length enum value string, which would throw as it was attempted to print.

I've changed the algorithm to "backoff" to `foo_bar`/`fooBar` delimited words. Some refactors too. I've ensured the output for examples in this repo hasn't changed.

Note that the value prefixing behavior is an approximation, and could delete more than desired, so I think this needs an optional override, like:
```sjson
enum_prefix_overrides = {
	"NvttContainer" = "NVTT_Container_"
	"b2HexColor" = "b2_color"
}
```

Alternatively, find a common prefix on the last `_`; this is convention, and works very well on the libraries I've tested, with the exception of a couple types in Box2D (`b2HexColor`, `b2TOIState`). That feels like an inconsistency on their part which could be patched with the above override.

## 🐞 버그 수정

```typescript
// 내 정보 API 호출로 accessToken 유효성 확인
const checkValidToken = async () => {
  try {
    const res = await fetch(`${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/v1/member/me`, {
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}`,
      },
    })

    const result = await res.json()

    if (result.result === 'SUCCESS') {
      isAuthenticated = true
    } else {
      shouldRemoveCookies = true
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.log('❌ Token 유효성 error:', error)
    shouldRemoveCookies = true
  }
}

if (accessToken) await checkValidToken()
```

